flowchart TB
  accTitle: Change contract for an agentic capability
  accDescr: A product decision defines allowed knowledge. Context and a typed proposal lead to deterministic validation. Outputs are classified into the correct record, persisted, projected under policy, delivered through interfaces, and verified. Observed behavior then informs the next bounded change.

  subgraph design["DESIGN THE DECISION"]
    direction LR
    Decide["1. Define decision and allowed knowledge"] --> Context["2. Build bounded context"]
    Context --> Type["3. Return a typed proposal"]
  end

  subgraph accept["ACCEPT AND RECORD"]
    direction LR
    Validate["4. Validate deterministically"] --> Classify["5. Classify the record"]
    Classify --> Persist["6. Persist before dependent publish"]
  end

  subgraph deliver["PROJECT AND VERIFY"]
    direction LR
    Project["7. Extend projections and policies"] --> Deliver["8. Deliver through REST, WebSocket, MCP, and web"]
    Deliver --> Verify["9. Test contracts; review simulations"]
  end

  Type --> Validate
  Persist --> Project
  Verify -. observed quality and failures .-> Decide

  class Decide,Context,Type designNode
  class Validate,Classify gateNode
  class Persist,Project deliveryNode
  class Deliver,Verify outputNode

